# A league's own artwork and templates. The folders are kept so a clone has somewhere
# obvious to put things; what goes in them is the league's and is never committed, so
# pulling an update to the bot cannot conflict with it. See resources/README.md.
#
# The two negations name **one** level deliberately, `*` and not `**`. A class folder is
# always exactly one deep, so `*` keeps every .gitkeep tracked while leaving anything
# nested below a class folder ignored. `**` un-ignored those deeper folders too, and a
# league that clones an artwork repository into one of them -- which is an ordinary thing
# to do -- then had it committed as a bare gitlink by the next `git add -A`: a pointer to
# a commit in a repository nobody else can reach, and an empty folder on a fresh clone.
resources/league/**
!resources/league/*/
!resources/league/*/.gitkeep
